NAME
       groupmod - change a group's name or ID

SYNOPSIS
       groupmod [-g GID] [-o] [-n NEW-NAME] GROUP

DESCRIPTION
       groupmod changes a group in /etc/group and /etc/gshadow. Changing the
       name keeps the members and the files. Changing the GID updates users
       whose primary group it is, but files on disk keep the old number;
       fix them with find / -gid OLD -exec chgrp NEWNAME {} \;.

       To change the members, use gpasswd or usermod -aG.

OPTIONS
       -g GID, --gid GID
              Give the group this ID.

       -n NAME, --new-name NAME
              Rename the group.

       -o, --non-unique
              With -g, allow an ID another group already has.

EXAMPLES
           groupmod -n developers devops
           groupmod -g 3001 developers

SEE ALSO
       groupadd(8), groupdel(8), gpasswd(1), usermod(8)
